\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {A wall visible in real encodings disappears in predicted rollouts.} A pre-reveal context is followed by futures under recorded actions: the simulator, decoded real JEPA encodings, decoded original JEPA predictions, and one flow-model sample. The JEPA rows use encoder seed 0 and the same fitted decoder. The example is the first stored diagnostic context at wall position $x=45$ among 64 contexts whose recorded futures survive the horizon. The flow sample is a single-checkpoint feasibility reference. A decoding failure on predicted latents can reflect both prediction error and off-distribution read-out; it is not alone proof of information loss.}}{24}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rollouts}{{6}{24}{\textbf {A wall visible in real encodings disappears in predicted rollouts.} A pre-reveal context is followed by futures under recorded actions: the simulator, decoded real JEPA encodings, decoded original JEPA predictions, and one flow-model sample. The JEPA rows use encoder seed 0 and the same fitted decoder. The example is the first stored diagnostic context at wall position $x=45$ among 64 contexts whose recorded futures survive the horizon. The flow sample is a single-checkpoint feasibility reference. A decoding failure on predicted latents can reflect both prediction error and off-distribution read-out; it is not alone proof of information loss}{figure.6}{}}
